          "level": 4,
          "title": "High Power Mercenary",
          "body": "**Ability Scores**\n\n| Strength\u000b(STR) | Dexterity\u000b(DEX) | Constitution\u000b(CON) | Fighting\u000b(FIG) | Intelligence\u000b(INT) | Wisdom\u000b(WIS) | Charisma\u000b(CHA) | Perception\u000b(PER) |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| 18 (+4) | 20 (+5) | 18 (+4) | 20 (+5) | 16 (+3) | 18 (+4) | 18 (+4) | 16 (+3) |\n\n**Power Tier:** High Power | **HP:** 90 | **Speed:** 40 ft | **Tier Bonus:** \\+4\n\n**Active Defense:** Parry/Block 22, Dodge 22, Willpower 21, Social 21 | **Attack Value:** 19\n\n**Power Sets:** Regeneration 3, Armor Systems 1, Super Senses 2 (Enhanced hearing, sight, smell), Martial Mastery 2\n\n- Regeneration: 1d12+CON \\[10\\] HP per Turn  \n- Powered claws: Attack \\+9 vs Parry/Block, 3d12+5 \\[24\\] slashing  \n- Energy rifle: Attack \\+9 vs Dodge, 3d12+5 \\[24\\] energy, Medium range  \n- Multiple grenade types (Encounter and Daily each): Restraint, Fire, Knockout gas  \n- Enhanced Senses: Cannot be surprised, Advantage on Notice, track by scent\n\n**Skills:** Acrobatics (trained, Advantage), Athletics (trained, Advantage), Stealth (trained), Notice (trained, Advantage) **Talents:** Ambidextrous, Master of Combat, Photographic Memory **Merits:** None | **Flaws:** Bad Reputation (Rating 2), Loner (Rating 1), Bounties and enemies (Rating 3\\)\n\n**Notes:** One of the most individually capable non-powered combatants at High Power. Regeneration means they must be overwhelmed sustainably. Enhanced senses mean ambushes rarely work. The combination of extreme individual competence and complete moral flexibility makes them the most dangerous mercenary archetype.\n\n---"
